Monitor social media sentiment regarding the stock market and specific S&P 500 companies. Use natural language processing (NLP) to analyze tweets, news articles, and forum posts. Distinguish between noise and genuine shifts in sentiment. Filter social media for relevant opinions, and cross validate with financial data and market fundamentals. Assign a sentiment score reflecting the aggregate social media sentiment, but apply a significant discount to its overall impact on the final prediction. Bias low conviction scores unless correlated to other factors.